h.\"}, {\"id\": \"s5\", \"text\": \"The university's sprawling campus, with its mix of colonial and modern architecture, had been her playground, where she would often get lost in the labyrinthine corridors, stumbling upon hidden courtyards and secret gardens.\"}, {\"id\": \"s6\", \"text\": \"One particular afternoon, while researching in the university's library, Petia had stumbled upon an obscure text by a 19th-century Mexican writer, which would later become the foundation of her dissertation.\"}, {\"id\": \"s7\", \"text\": \"The musty smell of the old book still lingered in her nostrils, transporting her back to that moment of discovery.\"}, {\"id\": \"s8\", \"text\": \"As she delved deeper into her research, Petia's fascination with the intersection of cultures and literatures only grew stronger.\"}, {\"id\": \"s9\", \"text\": \"Her time at the National Autonomous University of Mexico had instilled in her a sense of curiosity and adventure, which she carried with her to the University of Washington, where she would eventually earn her Ph.D.\"}, {\"id\": \"s10\", \"text\": \"in Comparative Literature.\"}, {\"id\": \"s11\", \"text\": \"The memories of those formative years still whispered in her ear, guiding her as she navigated the complex landscape of literary theory and criticism.\"}]}"
